<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary intervention.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary intervention.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico completed intervention on Friday by draining 3.658 billion pesos from the secondary market through a combination of three direct sales of paper and six repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    363 days   23.25 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    181 days   22.48 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days   22.27 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    550 million     39 days   22.60 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     31 days   22.30 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     20 days   22.35 pct</p>
<p>    650 million     10 days   23.40 pct</p>
<p>    650 million	6 days   23.73 pct</p>
<p>    158 million	1 day    23.40 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
